      "problem": "Simplify the expression $(A∧B)∨(A∧¬B).$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's simplify the expression using the properties of logical operations:\n\n- First,  we use the distributive law (conjunction over disjunction):\n\n$$\n(A∧B)∨(A∧¬B)≡A∧(B∨¬B)\n$$\n\n- Next,  we use the fact that the disjunction of an expression and its negation is a tautology:\n\n$$\nA∧(B∨¬B)≡A∧\\text{t}\n$$\n\n- Finally, we use the fact that the conjunction of an expression and a tautology gives the initial expression:\n\n$$\nA∧\\text{t}≡A\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n(A∧B)∨(A∧¬B)≡A.\n$$",
